{"nodes": [{"id": "questions_25_challenges_faced_question", "label": "Q25: Challenges faced with microservices", "file_type": "document", "source_file": "docs/questions/25-challenges-faced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null}, {"id": "questions_25_challenges_faced_bugs_in_the_seams", "label": "The bugs are in the seams", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/questions/25-challenges-faced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Almost none are caught by unit tests; every real problem came from running the system, not from a red test. Unit tests cover the least risky part, which is why the messaging tier is the second-largest test tier."}, {"id": "questions_25_challenges_faced_silent_participant_bug", "label": "Bug: a silent saga participant hung the orchestrator", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/questions/25-challenges-faced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "WithdrawRiskRegisterConsumer returned early when there was nothing to withdraw \u2014 which reads as sensible defensive programming and hangs the saga to its 30-second timeout. Lesson: in a saga, silence is a failure mode."}, {"id": "questions_25_challenges_faced_counter_drift_bug", "label": "Bug: a projection that could not tell a recovery from a new reading", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/questions/25-challenges-faced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "RAG buckets kept as increment/decrement counters broke when a KPI recovered, because the event carries the new status but not the old. Fixed by a per-KPI status row and recomputation."}, {"id": "questions_25_challenges_faced_correlation_id_bug", "label": "Bug: a correlation id that vanished at the first hop", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/questions/25-challenges-faced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "A reverse proxy forwards the incoming headers and nothing had written the generated id back onto the request. Lesson: a correlation id that is only logged locally is a request id; propagation has to be tested end to end."}, {"id": "questions_25_challenges_faced_provider_behaviour_bug", "label": "Bug: provider behaviour invisible until it runs", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/questions/25-challenges-faced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "SQLite cannot ORDER BY a DateTimeOffset, and only an INTEGER primary key autoincrements \u2014 which forced the outbox's ordering column to become its key. The fix belongs in shared infrastructure as a convention-applied value converter, not in each query."}, {"id": "questions_25_challenges_faced_string_length_asymmetry_bug", "label": "Bug: shared code failing in one service and not its neighbour", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/questions/25-challenges-faced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "An instance id truncated with [..48] throws if the string is shorter, and issues-api is two characters shorter than projects-api. That asymmetry is very hard to reason about from a stack trace."}, {"id": "questions_25_challenges_faced_token_relay_bug", "label": "Bug: the same identity bug twice, in two outbound clients", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/questions/25-challenges-faced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The gateway aggregation endpoint and, weeks later, the read-model rebuild endpoint both called downstream services anonymously. Lesson: when changing a cross-cutting concern, ask which other outbound clients exist \u2014 a grep for AddHttpClient would have found both in seconds."}, {"id": "questions_25_challenges_faced_rabbitmq_outage_demo", "label": "The unplanned RabbitMQ outage that proved the outbox", "file_type": "concept", "source_file": "docs/questions/25-challenges-faced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The broker container restarted mid-verification; services stayed healthy, HTTP writes kept succeeding, two events sat unpublished, and the saga completed one second after the broker returned with nothing lost. Without the outbox those events would have been published into a dead connection and gone."}, {"id": "questions_25_challenges_faced_build_the_platform_first", "label": "Build the platform before the second service", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/questions/25-challenges-faced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "Outbox, inbox, correlation, health and resilience retrofitted across nine services is much worse than having them from the start, which is why they are the phase-1 commit. Also: start with a modular monolith, design events to be idempotent rather than only consumers, and write the failure test first \u2014 the saga tests written failure-first found nothing later because those bugs were never written."}, {"id": "questions_25_challenges_faced_operational_over_architectural", "label": "The difficulty is operational, not architectural", "file_type": "rationale", "source_file": "docs/questions/25-challenges-faced.md", "source_location": null, "source_url": null, "captured_at": null, "author": null, "contributor": null, "rationale": "The patterns are well documented and not hard to implement; knowing that a queue is quietly growing at 3am or that a saga has been stuck since Tuesday is the part that takes real work. Local development also gets heavier, mitigated by test tiers that need zero infrastructure and run in ~11 seconds."}], "edges": [{"source": "questions_25_challenges_faced_bugs_in_the_seams", "target": "questions_25_challenges_faced_question", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/questions/25-challenges-faced.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "questions_25_challenges_faced_silent_participant_bug", "target": "questions_25_challenges_faced_bugs_in_the_seams", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/questions/25-challenges-faced.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "questions_25_challenges_faced_counter_drift_bug", "target": "questions_25_challenges_faced_bugs_in_the_seams", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/questions/25-challenges-faced.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "questions_25_challenges_faced_correlation_id_bug", "target": "questions_25_challenges_faced_bugs_in_the_seams", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/questions/25-challenges-faced.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "questions_25_challenges_faced_provider_behaviour_bug", "target": "questions_25_challenges_faced_bugs_in_the_seams", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/questions/25-challenges-faced.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "questions_25_challenges_faced_string_length_asymmetry_bug", "target": "questions_25_challenges_faced_bugs_in_the_seams", "relation": "references", "confidence": "EXTRACTED", "confidence_score": 1.0, "source_file": "docs/questions/25-challenges-faced.md", "source_location": null, "weight": 1.0}, {"source": "questions_25_challenges_face